# Migrations — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Versioned SQL migrations applied with the `sqlx` CLI.

## Setup

```bash
cargo install sqlx-cli --no-default-features --features rustls,postgres
```

`sqlx` reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment or `.env`.

## Usage

```bash
sqlx migrate add create_tours   # writes migrations/<timestamp>_create_tours.sql
sqlx migrate run                # applies everything pending
sqlx migrate info               # shows applied vs pending
```

## Rules

- Migrations are append-only. Never edit one that has run anywhere but your own
  machine — `sqlx` records a checksum per migration and refuses to run when an
  applied file has changed.
- To undo a shipped migration, write a new one that reverses it.
- Every migration must be reviewable on its own. No `DROP` without an explicit note
  in the pull request describing what data disappears.
